{
  "abstract": "In a finite split graph whose host neighborhoods are independent in the residual core graph, a proper assignment missing L required pairs realizes the residual integral-fractional packing gap to within 2L. Deleting q crossing edges from a complete assignment changes the gap by at most 2q. For a split presentation with core size c and at least 2c hosts, the gap is at most twice the sum of endpoint omissions in excess of floor(c/2).",
  "authors": [
    {
      "name": "Juan Pablo Traverso Gianini"
    }
